# catalog — public package list
File: website/pulled/catalog.oot

Source: openOODA/catalog/docs/

## What it is

The public list of openOODA packages. It is a file tree, not a
registry service. No accounts. No daemon.

Host: `https://catalog.openooda.org`

`opm search` reads the `catalog` file. `opm add` installs a
child folder (manifest plus `.oo` payload).

## Use

```
opm search hello
opm add hello
```

The opm repo ships the same packages under `seed/`. Search
reads seed first, so `opm search hello` works with no
network. This catalog repo is the copy the world can fetch.
HTTPS fetch needs `OODA_CURL`. HTTPS add also verifies
`index.minisig` with the stock pubkey.

## Surface

Stock packages:

| Name | Version | Caps |
|------|---------|------|
| hello | 0.1.0 | FsRead |
| echo | 0.1.0 | FsRead |

Index lines are `name|version|caps|deps|sha256`. Each child
folder holds `manifest` plus the payload named in `payload=`.

Add a package by committing a folder, rebuilding `catalog`
with `opm bot`, and signing `index.minisig`. Git tags are
the version (RFC-0006). There is no VERSION file.
